"""
apex-agent v3.0 — Sovereign Agentic Coding & Swarm Execution Engine for Apex Terminal OS
Engineered exclusively for Rick Jefferson | RJ Business Solutions
Features:
  - Parallel Tool Execution (ThreadPoolExecutor concurrent reads, searches, and fetches)
  - Subagent Parallel Swarm (spawn_parallel_workers for disjoint subtasks)
  - 13-Tool Professional Arsenal (ripgrep, git diff, web scraper, AppleScript GUI, memory)
  - Multi-Provider Failover Chain (Venice AI -> Sovereign GLM -> OpenRouter -> Local Ollama $0)
  - Auto-Retry with Exponential Backoff on HTTP 429 rate limits
  - Claude Code / OpenCode compatibility: reads both AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md + persistent SQLite memory
  - Self-Healing Verification Loop & Epistemic Barrier Discipline

Usage:
  apex-agent "fix the failing test in tests/"
  apex-agent --parallel 8 "audit the codebase and find all deprecated APIs"
  apex-agent --plan "add rate limiting to the API"       # plan first, execute on approval
  apex-agent --trust yolo "refactor the auth module"     # hands-free zero-nag mode
  apex-agent --swarm "audit frontend, backend, and db"   # parallel subagent swarm
  apex-agent --model ollama "explain this codebase"      # $0 local offline mode

Aliases (wired in ~/.zshrc):
  ax    "task"   -> apex-agent "task"
  axp   "task"   -> apex-agent --plan "task"
  axy   "task"   -> apex-agent --trust yolo "task"
  axpar "task"   -> apex-agent --parallel 8 "task"
  axswarm "task" -> apex-agent --swarm "task"

Config (optional) in project root `.apexagent` (JSON):
  {"model": "zai-org-glm-5-2", "trust": "ask", "max_steps": 40, "parallel": 8, "allow_cmds": ["pytest", "npm test", "git status"]}
"""

